       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day for adults. Higher doses add more edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia without much more blood pressure lowering.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n- **Enter 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a common starting dose, and you can titrate up.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough, an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is usually better than a higher amlodipine dose.\n- **Enter 20 mg as written.** If you want this on purpose, for example for a specific clinical reason, confirm and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's an intentional above-maximum dose.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
